# Copilot governance ownership
#
# prompt-core and hooks are the reason this file matters most. prompt-core
# contains executable code that runs on the developer's machine on every prompt,
# and the policy rule set that decides what is blocked. hooks registers that
# code with the IDE. A change to either alters what executes on every developer
# workstation, so both require security review in every repository — not just
# in the central governance repository.
.github/copilot-instructions.md      @org/platform-architecture @org/security
.github/instructions/**              @org/platform-architecture @org/security
.github/prompt-core/**               @org/platform-architecture @org/security
.github/hooks/**                     @org/platform-architecture @org/security
.github/prompts/**                   @org/platform-architecture
